    {
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        224,
        224
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Settings for this workflow (labels, filter lists, defaults, owner). Other nodes read\n// $('Config').first().json; the build injects config/config.local.json here.\n// @inject config as CONFIG\n// @end-inject\nreturn [{ json: CONFIG }];\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Prefilter",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        448,
        224
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "const CONFIG = $('Config').first().json;\n// @inject src/prefilter.js as prefilter\n// @end-inject\n// Rule pre-filter: excluded and ignored senders never reach a model (hard rule 7);\n// mass mail (newsletters, promotions) is dropped here too, no model call, no Notion row.\nconst out = [];\n$input.all().forEach((item, idx) => {\n  const m = item.json;\n  const fromRaw =\n    typeof m.from === 'string'\n      ? m.from\n      : (m.from && (m.from.text || (m.from.value && m.from.value[0] && m.from.value[0].address))) || (m.headers && m.headers.from) || '';\n  const subject = m.subject || (m.headers && m.headers.subject) || '';\n  // Headers, text and html let the prefilter drop mass mail without a model call.\n  const verdict = prefilter.prefilterEmail({ from: fromRaw, subject, headers: m.headers, text: m.text, html: m.html }, CONFIG.filters);\n  if (verdict.action === 'drop') return;\n  const raw = m.text || m.textAsHtml || m.snippet || '';\n  const body = prefilter.trimBody(String(raw).replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' '), CONFIG.defaults.email_body_max_chars);\n  const channel = verdict.action;\n  out.push({\n    json: {\n      message_id: m.id,\n      thread_id: m.threadId,\n      source_id: (channel === 'linkedin' ? 'linkedin:' : 'gmail:') + m.id,\n      source: channel === 'linkedin' ? 'LinkedIn' : 'Gmail',\n      channel,\n      from: fromRaw,\n      address: verdict.address,\n      subject,\n      received: m.date || (m.headers && m.headers.date) || new Date().toISOString(),\n      body,\n      link: 'https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#inbox/' + m.threadId,\n    },\n    pairedItem: { item: idx },\n  });\n});\nreturn out;\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Triage agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        896,
        112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Today: {{ $now.setZone($('Config').first().json.timezone).toFormat('yyyy-LL-dd') }}\nChannel: {{ $json.channel }}\nFrom: {{ $json.from }}\nSubject: {{ $json.subject }}\nReceived: {{ $json.received }}\n\n{{ $json.body }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You sort incoming messages for {{ $('Config').first().json.owner.name }}. {{ $('Config').first().json.owner.context }}\n\nFor each message decide:\n1. action_needed: does it require anything from the owner? Replies a person is waiting for, deadlines, invitations that need an answer, requests, forms, payments: true. Newsletters, notifications, receipts, confirmations with nothing to do, marketing: false. A message from a person that only confirms something already arranged (a lesson, a meeting link, a booking, a reminder of a planned event) is not an action unless it asks a question or needs a decision. When unsure whether a human is waiting for an answer, prefer true: missing a reply costs more than one extra task.\n2. action_type: \"email_reply\" when answering this email by email is the only thing to do (only for channel \"email\"; for \"linkedin\" the reply happens inside LinkedIn, so use \"other\"); \"other\" when there is something else to do (prepare, book, pay, fill a form, reply on another channel), even if a reply is also expected; \"none\" when no action is needed.\n3. needs_reply: true when this email itself should be answered by email, whatever action_type says (only for channel \"email\"). An email that asks for both an answer and some work is action_type \"other\" with needs_reply true. False for newsletters, notifications and anything that expects no answer.\n4. priority: \"P1\" urgent and important (a person is waiting, interview logistics, a deadline within two days); \"P2\" important this week; \"P3\" can wait; \"\" when no action is needed.\n5. estimate_min: 15, 30, 60 or 120 minutes of the owner's time; 0 when no action is needed.\n6. fyi, only if no action is needed: true when the message is personally addressed to the owner or concerns the owner directly, and the owner would want one line about it in the morning digest: a delivery or appointment today, a payment or booking confirmation, a document that is ready, a note from a person that needs no answer. False for newsletters, promotions, marketing, product updates, social notifications, generic announcements, verification codes, anything sent to a list. When action is needed, false.\n7. confidence: your probability, from 0 to 1, that action_needed is correct.\n\nIf action is needed, also write the task:\n- title: a short imperative title in {{ $('Config').first().json.language.titles === 'ru' ? 'Russian' : 'English' }}, at most 80 characters, starting with a verb. For a reply on another channel start with the channel, for example \"Reply on LinkedIn: ...\". When the message needs both an answer and some other work, the task is the work; the reply is drafted separately, so do not make \"reply\" the title.\n- summary: one or two sentences in the same language: who wants what, and by when if stated. Facts only from the message; no greetings, signatures or quoted history.\n- due: the deadline as YYYY-MM-DD if the message states or clearly implies it, resolved against today's date given in the message; otherwise \"\". Never invent a deadline.\n- priority_reason: one short line in the same language explaining the urgency.\nIf no action is needed, title, summary, due and priority_reason are \"\".\n\nIf needs_reply is true or action_type is \"email_reply\", also write draft_body: a reply draft in the language of the incoming email. Tone: {{ $('Config').first().json.owner.tone }} Short and specific: answer what was asked, propose a concrete next step, no filler. Never invent facts, dates, numbers, availability, prices or commitments; where information is missing insert a placeholder such as [[date?]] or [[confirm?]] and set draft_needs_input to true. Do not accept or decline offers, interviews or payments on the owner's behalf unless the email leaves only one sensible answer. Plain text, ending with the signature: {{ $('Config').first().json.owner.signature }}. Otherwise draft_body is \"\" and draft_needs_input is false.\n\nChannel notes. email: automated senders (no-reply addresses, notifications) rarely need action unless they carry a deadline or a form only the owner can complete; shop notifications and generic updates are noise, not fyi. linkedin: notification emails, often only a snippet; InMails and recruiter messages that expect an answer need action, connection requests, reactions, post notifications and \"people you may know\" do not.\n\nYou only propose. The draft is saved as a Gmail draft for the owner to review; nothing is sent.",
          "maxIterations": 3,
          "enableStreaming": false
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
